== ψ-Dependent Extensions ==

=== TPMS Geometry as ψ Mode Selector ===

The [[ψ Metamaterials]] (B9) page develops the hypothesis that TPMS topologies correspond to specific ψ mode classes via the [[OSGS]] primitive symbol framework. Within this framework, the Gyroid (genus 3, chiral) and Schwarz-P (genus 3, achiral) are not simply two fabrication options — they are two geometrically distinct mode-selection operators. A device built on a Gyroid substrate preferentially supports different ψ mode families than the same device built on a Schwarz-P substrate.

If this hypothesis is confirmed at TML-1 (different S21 spectra for Gyroid vs Schwarz-P samples of identical fill), it would mean that the lattice topology selection is a primary [[Psi-Tech]] design parameter — not a manufacturing convenience — and that the six TPMS topology classes correspond to six distinct ψ mode-selection operators in the Base-216 symbolic system.

=== Topological Phase Boundaries ===

At the transition between different <math>t</math> values in a graded-t lattice, the TPMS topology changes continuously but its genus may jump discontinuously at certain critical values of <math>t</math>. These topological phase boundaries could produce ψ mode-conversion effects — a ψ wave propagating through the shell would partially convert from one mode family to another at each boundary. Engineered arrangements of topological boundaries could function as mode routers or ψ beam splitters, without any external switching.

== TML Measurement Protocol ==

=== TML-1 — Lattice Characterisation (No Subjects) ===

Print 5 sample cubes (10 mm × 10 mm × 10 mm) per batch at target <math>t</math> value. Measure:

# '''Density:''' Archimedes immersion method in isopropanol. Target: within ±3% of computed <math>\rho_{\rm rel}</math>.
# '''S-parameters:''' Mount sample in calibrated coaxial fixture (Damaskos M07 or equivalent). Measure S11, S21 from 1 kHz to 10 MHz using VNA (Keysight E5071C). Apply Nicholson–Ross–Weir algorithm to extract complex <math>\varepsilon_{\rm eff}(\omega)</math> and <math>\mu_{\rm eff}(\omega)</math>.
# '''Mechanical:''' Uniaxial compression test (Instron 5965). Extract Young's modulus and yield stress. Target: Young's modulus > 0.5 GPa at <math>t = 0.4</math>, yield stress > 5 MPa.
# '''Channel integrity:''' Pressure test ferrofluid channels at 2 bar with dyed water. No leakage into pore volume.

'''Pass criteria:''' Measured <math>\varepsilon_{\rm eff}</math> within 15% of Maxwell-Garnett prediction; mechanical targets met; zero channel leakage.

=== TML-2 — Coil Integration (No Subjects) ===

Integrate bifilar coil into printed shell. Measure:
# E-field distribution via near-field probe (Langer EMV RF-B3 or equivalent) on scanning stage at 5 mm above shell surface.
# Compare against COMSOL EM simulation prediction. Agreement target: < 20% RMS deviation across field map.
# ICNIRP E-field compliance: maximum measured field at 10 cm from shell must be below 83 V/m (ICNIRP 2010, 40 kHz reference level).

